# Reviewed tenant-filter bypasses. Format: repository-relative path|method-call count|why the bypass is required.
# Counts include only IgnoreQueryFilters() calls, not comments or documentation. Any count change requires review.
ProjectBeacon.API/Auth/ApiTokenAuthMiddleware.cs|9|Authenticates API tokens and resolves device, chat, task, and run ownership before tenant scope is bound; each lookup is constrained by the token or validated actor resource.
ProjectBeacon.Application/Agents/ApplyAgentConfigHandler.cs|1|Resolves the project membership needed to authorize an agent configuration apply before project scope is available.
ProjectBeacon.Application/Agents/ModelBackendHandlers.cs|2|Checks cross-project membership and role bindings while authorizing model backend changes.
ProjectBeacon.Application/Agents/ProjectMcpServerHandlers.cs|2|Loads project-scoped MCP configuration after validating the project requested by the caller.
ProjectBeacon.Application/Auth/LoginHandlers.cs|16|Accepts invite and login flows using opaque invite credentials, then validates invite, organization, and project membership relationships explicitly. Invite-based registration rechecks lifecycle and invitation state under the shared organization capacity lock and enforces the same member-seat reservation before creating a user or membership.
ProjectBeacon.Application/Authorization/AuthorizationService.cs|11|Implements central authorization by resolving the actor's project and organization memberships across tenant boundaries.
ProjectBeacon.Application/Chat/ChatHandlers.cs|8|Resolves chat sessions, parts, and project membership by explicit session and actor identifiers for authenticated chat operations.
ProjectBeacon.Application/Devices/CommandCompletions.cs|11|Processes device-owned commands and associated pipeline, chat, eval, and review state after validating command, device, project, and generation identifiers; Actor failure completion also resolves its pinned subtask/session and writes the server-owned task workspace report within the command's project scope.
ProjectBeacon.Application/Devices/CommandRecovery.cs|1|Recovers stale pipeline work by its persisted command/session identifiers across the request tenant boundary.
ProjectBeacon.Application/Devices/DesiredState.cs|2|Updates desired device and project-runtime revisions for the explicitly selected device or project.
ProjectBeacon.Application/Devices/DeviceLifecycleHandlers.cs|2|Creates and maintains device identity and runtime links after validating the owning user and project references.
ProjectBeacon.Application/Devices/DeviceLlamaSwapProxy.cs|2|Resolves the device's active project runtimes and memberships before proxying the authorized model operation.
ProjectBeacon.Application/Devices/HarnessTokenCommands.cs|9|Authenticates harness tokens and resolves their explicit device, command, chat, task, subtask, eval, and project scopes.
ProjectBeacon.Application/Devices/ProjectRuntimeHandlers.cs|11|Creates, attaches, detaches, and reports project runtime links after explicitly checking project membership, admin role, and device ownership.
ProjectBeacon.Application/Devices/ProjectRuntimeResolver.cs|2|Resolves runtime assignment for a known project or device using explicit project and device identifiers.
ProjectBeacon.Application/Devices/WorkstationCommandHandlers.cs|7|Claims and completes commands for an authenticated device and validates the associated task, session, subtask, project, and command generation.
ProjectBeacon.Application/Evals/EvalPairHandler.cs|3|Loads and authorizes eval task, project membership, and pinned run state for the explicitly selected eval.
ProjectBeacon.Application/Identity/CurrentProjectLookup.cs|10|Finds the current actor's project and organization memberships before a tenant context has been selected, including organization-only fallback for invited owners without a project; each lookup is constrained by the user id and, when supplied, the preferred project or organization id.
ProjectBeacon.Application/Identity/InviteHandlers.cs|37|Resolves and manages organization/project invitations only by opaque token hash or explicit invite, project, organization, and user identifiers; authorization and lifecycle checks precede exposed reads or mutations, writes are re-read in the invite's bound tenant, and member-capacity checks explicitly count active members and valid seat reservations. Create/accept/revoke operations recheck organization lifecycle and current authorization under the shared entitlement lock to serialize state changes and seat reservations.
ProjectBeacon.Application/Projects/ApiTokenHandlers.cs|2|Lists and revokes API tokens by explicit token and owner identifiers, including tokens outside the default project filter.
ProjectBeacon.Application/Projects/ProjectHandlers.cs|11|Authorizes project administration and performs project-scoped dependent cleanup after loading the explicitly requested project.
ProjectBeacon.Application/Projects/ProjectQueries.cs|13|Lists projects and associated task, milestone, session, and section summaries visible to the current actor across their memberships.
ProjectBeacon.Application/Tasks/PipelineControlHandlers.cs|1|Loads review-run state by explicit task and project identifiers during a guarded pipeline control operation.
ProjectBeacon.Application/Tasks/PipelineFormHandlers.cs|5|Resolves pipeline form sessions, tasks, devices, and membership for a reply bound to an explicit project session.
ProjectBeacon.Application/Tasks/PipelineLifecycleHandlers.cs|2|Resolves project runtime and device assignments before pipeline session launch.
ProjectBeacon.Application/Tasks/PipelineQueryHandlers.cs|2|Builds pipeline preflight by loading runtime devices explicitly assigned to the selected project.
ProjectBeacon.Application/Tasks/PipelineSupport.cs|10|Builds pipeline state from commands, sessions, devices, and review runs restricted by the selected task and project identifiers.
ProjectBeacon.Application/Tasks/TaskLifecycleHandlers.cs|6|Performs task deletion and dependent cleanup across project-scoped related entities after authorizing the selected task.
ProjectBeacon.Web/Extensions/CircuitTenantRevalidation.cs|2|Revalidates the authenticated user identity across tenant boundaries and re-reads the selected organization's lifecycle by explicit user and organization identifiers when a Blazor circuit changes its active tenant.
ProjectBeacon.Web/Extensions/EndpointExtensions.cs|1|Checks the selected target organization's lifecycle before switching into it, including when the current tenant-scoped organization filter intentionally hides suspended and closed tenants.
ProjectBeacon.Infrastructure/Http/TenantIsolationMiddleware.cs|6|Resolves the authenticated tenant scope before tenant filters are activated; project and organization memberships, requested project/org matching, API-token project-to-org binding, and the selected organization's lifecycle status are explicitly constrained by authenticated user, device/token resource, or requested scope.
ProjectBeacon.Application/Devices/ProjectGitSyncHandlers.cs|5|Selects the project's runtime and online capability-advertising device across tenant filters, loads the explicitly requested project for its audit envelope, and reads only the GitSync command bound to the authorized project; each query is constrained by the route projectId and, for the command, the exact commandId and kind.
ProjectBeacon.Application/Identity/TenantContextBinder.cs|1|Resolves the authenticated user's current project and organization membership before the request tenant context has been bound.
ProjectBeacon.Infrastructure/Entitlements/PostgresEntitlementService.cs|1|Reads the effective entitlement for an explicit organization before deciding whether tenant access is allowed.
ProjectBeacon.Infrastructure/Organizations/EfOrganizationAdminService.cs|22|Performs Control Plane authorized organization, membership, invitation, account, and audit operations across customer tenant scopes. Operator-issued owner invitations re-read active members and pending seat reservations under the shared organization capacity lock.
ProjectBeacon.Infrastructure/Organizations/EfOrganizationDataExportService.cs|3|Re-reads the explicitly authorized organization and enumerates that organization’s projects in a consistent export snapshot; all subsequent project-scoped datasets are constrained by those project ids and related task/decision ids.
